    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">International marketing</span> is the application of marketing principles to sell goods and services across national borders. As businesses grow, many seek opportunities beyond their domestic market to increase sales and profitability.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning and Scope of International Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">International marketing involves planning and conducting transactions across national boundaries to satisfy the needs of consumers in more than one country. Its scope covers export/import trade, foreign direct investment, licensing, franchising, and joint ventures with foreign partners.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Importance of International Marketing</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Benefit</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Foreign exchange earnings</td><td>Exports bring in foreign currency needed for imports and development</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Market expansion</td><td>Businesses can grow sales beyond a limited domestic market</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economies of scale</td><td>Larger markets allow firms to produce more and reduce cost per unit</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Access to resources</td><td>Countries can access raw materials/technology not available locally</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Employment creation</td><td>Export industries create jobs domestically</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Challenges Faced by Nigerian Marketers</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Nigerian exporters often face challenges such as poor infrastructure (power, ports, roads), stringent international quality/standard requirements, currency instability, high tariffs and trade barriers in foreign markets, limited access to international market information, and strong competition from established global brands.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember the key distinction: international marketing is not just "exporting" — it also includes licensing, franchising, joint ventures, and foreign direct investment as methods of entering foreign markets.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> International marketing extends marketing activities across national borders through exports, licensing, franchising, joint ventures, and investment. It brings benefits like foreign exchange and market expansion but Nigerian marketers face challenges of infrastructure, standards, and currency instability.\n</div>\n  ',
