    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Information and Communication Technology (ICT)</span> has transformed how businesses market their products across borders, making international trade faster, cheaper, and accessible even to small businesses.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of ICT in Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">ICT refers to technologies — computers, the internet, mobile devices, software — used to create, store, exchange, and use information. In marketing, ICT enables businesses to reach global customers, process transactions, and manage international operations digitally.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Roles of ICT in Modern International Marketing</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>E-commerce</td><td>Buying and selling goods/services online (e.g., via websites, marketplaces like Alibaba, Amazon)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Online advertising</td><td>Promoting products to global audiences via social media, search engines, and websites</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Digital payments</td><td>Enabling fast, secure cross-border transactions (e.g., PayPal, bank transfers)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Market research</td><td>Using online tools/analytics to study foreign consumer behavior and trends</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Communication</td><td>Instant communication with foreign partners/customers via email, video calls, messaging apps</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Benefits of ICT to International Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">ICT reduces the cost of reaching foreign markets, allows even small businesses to sell internationally without a physical foreign presence, speeds up transactions and communication, provides real-time market data, and enables 24/7 accessibility to global customers.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Challenges of Applying ICT</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Challenges include limited internet access/infrastructure in some areas, cybersecurity risks (fraud, hacking), digital literacy gaps among traders, and the cost of setting up e-commerce platforms and digital payment systems.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners often test the specific ICT tools (e-commerce, online advertising, digital payments) rather than the general concept. Know real examples like Alibaba, Amazon, and mobile money platforms.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> ICT enables e-commerce, online advertising, digital payments, market research, and instant communication in international marketing, drastically lowering the cost and difficulty of reaching foreign markets, though infrastructure and cybersecurity challenges remain.\n</div>\n  ',
