      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Before opening a shop, stall, or any <span class="learn-keyword">personal marketing outlet</span>, careful planning is essential. Poor planning is one of the leading causes of small business failure.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Steps in Establishing a Personal Marketing Outlet</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Key Consideration</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Location</td><td>Choose a site with good customer traffic, accessibility, and appropriate rent</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Capital</td><td>Determine how much money is needed to start and sustain the business</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Staffing</td><td>Decide how many employees are needed and their required skills</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Product selection</td><td>Choose products that meet local demand and offer good profit margins</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Legal requirements</td><td>Register the business and obtain any necessary permits/licenses</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Importance of Location</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Location determines how easily customers can find and access the outlet. A good location has high foot traffic, visibility, adequate parking/access, security, and proximity to the target customer base.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Determining Capital Requirements</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Capital needs include the cost of rent/lease, initial stock/inventory, shop fittings and equipment, staff salaries, licensing fees, and a reserve for unforeseen expenses. Underestimating capital needs is a common cause of business failure.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Risks and Management</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Common risks include theft, fire, poor sales, spoilage of perishable stock, and competition. These can be managed through insurance, proper security measures, careful inventory control, and continuous monitoring of sales performance.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners like to test the ORDER of planning steps. Remember: assess location and capital needs FIRST, before finalizing staffing and product selection.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Planning a personal marketing outlet involves carefully choosing a location, determining capital requirements, deciding on staffing, and selecting the right products, while proactively identifying and managing business risks.\n</div>\n  ',
