    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Purchasing</span>, <span class="learn-keyword">supplying</span>, and <span class="learn-keyword">merchandising</span> are interconnected activities that ensure the right goods reach the right place, in the right condition, ready for sale.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Purchasing and Supplying</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Purchasing</strong> is the process of buying goods or services needed by a business, involving selecting suppliers, negotiating prices, and ensuring quality. <strong>Supplying</strong> is the process of providing/delivering those goods to where they are needed, such as from a wholesaler to a retailer.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Meaning of Merchandising</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Merchandising refers to all the activities involved in promoting and presenting products to customers at the point of sale to encourage purchase — including product display, pricing, signage, and store layout.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Methods of Merchandising</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Visual merchandising</td><td>Attractive product displays, window dressing, shelf arrangement</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Point-of-sale promotion</td><td>In-store discounts, signage, and demonstrations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cross-merchandising</td><td>Displaying related products together (e.g., bread next to butter)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Digital merchandising</td><td>Online product listings, photos, and descriptions on e-commerce sites</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Importance of Merchandising in Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Effective merchandising increases sales by attracting customer attention, improves the shopping experience, helps move slow-selling stock, builds brand image, and encourages impulse buying.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Do not confuse purchasing (buying inputs) with merchandising (presenting/promoting products for sale). Purchasing happens before the product reaches the shop floor; merchandising happens at the point of sale.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Purchasing is buying needed goods, supplying is delivering them to where needed, and merchandising is presenting and promoting them at the point of sale. Together, these functions ensure goods are available, in the right place, and attractively presented to boost sales.\n</div>\n  ',
