    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Not everything sold in the market is a physical product. <span class="learn-keyword">Services</span> — like banking, transportation, education, and hairdressing — are intangible offerings that require their own unique marketing approach.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Services</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A service is an intangible activity or benefit that one party offers to another, which does not result in the ownership of anything physical. Examples include banking, healthcare, education, transportation, and hospitality.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Characteristics of Services (the "4 I\'s")</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Characteristic</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Intangibility</td><td>Services cannot be seen, touched, or held before purchase</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inseparability</td><td>Production and consumption of a service happen at the same time (e.g., a haircut)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inconsistency (Variability)</td><td>Quality of service can vary between providers or even between visits</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inventory (Perishability)</td><td>Services cannot be stored for later use — an empty hotel room tonight is lost revenue forever</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Types of Services</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Services can be classified as consumer services (e.g., salon, restaurant), business/professional services (e.g., legal, accounting, consulting), and public services (e.g., healthcare, education provided by government).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Problems and Prospects of Marketing Services</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Problems include the difficulty of demonstrating quality before purchase (due to intangibility), inconsistency in service delivery, and difficulty in pricing. Prospects include the growing service sector\'s contribution to GDP, opportunities in digital/online services, and increasing demand for professional and personal services as economies develop.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Memorize the four characteristics of services (Intangibility, Inseparability, Inconsistency, Inventory/Perishability) — these are frequently tested individually with real-life examples.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Services are intangible offerings characterized by intangibility, inseparability, inconsistency, and perishability. Marketing services requires building trust and consistent quality since customers cannot inspect a service before buying it, unlike physical goods.\n</div>\n  ',
