    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Consumer behavior</span> is the study of how individuals decide to search for, purchase, use, and dispose of products and services. Understanding it helps marketers design better products, pricing, and promotions.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Consumer Behavior</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Consumer behavior examines the actions and decision-making processes people go through when choosing what to buy, including the psychological, social, and economic influences behind those choices.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Factors Affecting Consumer Behavior</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cultural</td><td>Traditions, values, religion, and customs of the society</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Social</td><td>Family, friends, reference groups, and social class</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Psychological</td><td>Motivation, perception, learning, beliefs, and attitudes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economic</td><td>Income level, price of goods, and purchasing power</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Consumer Decision-Making Process</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The typical process follows five stages: (1) Problem/need recognition, (2) Information search, (3) Evaluation of alternatives, (4) Purchase decision, and (5) Post-purchase evaluation (satisfaction or regret, which affects future purchases).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Why Marketers Study Consumer Behavior</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Understanding consumer behavior helps marketers design products that meet real needs, set appropriate prices, choose effective promotional messages, select the right distribution channels, and build long-term customer loyalty.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Learn the five stages of the decision-making process in order — this sequence is a favorite exam question. Remember: Need Recognition → Information Search → Evaluation → Purchase → Post-Purchase.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Consumer behavior studies how cultural, social, psychological, and economic factors shape buying decisions, which follow a five-stage process from need recognition to post-purchase evaluation. Marketers use this understanding to design better products and marketing strategies.\n</div>\n  ',
