    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Price</span> is the amount of money charged for a product or service. Choosing the right pricing policy is a critical marketing decision that affects sales volume, profit, and how customers perceive a product.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Pricing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Pricing is the process of determining the value a company will receive in exchange for its products or services. It must balance covering costs, earning profit, and remaining attractive/competitive to target customers.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Types of Pricing Policies/Strategies</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Penetration pricing</td><td>Setting a low initial price to quickly attract customers and gain market share</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Skimming pricing</td><td>Setting a high initial price to maximize profit from early adopters before lowering it later</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cost-plus pricing</td><td>Adding a fixed markup percentage to the cost of producing the item</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Competitive pricing</td><td>Setting prices based on what competitors charge for similar products</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Factors Influencing Pricing Decisions</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Key factors include production costs, level of competition, target customers\' ability and willingness to pay, government regulations/taxes, the product\'s stage in its life cycle, and overall company objectives (e.g., maximizing market share vs. maximizing profit).</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Don\'t mix up penetration pricing (LOW price to enter market/gain share) with skimming pricing (HIGH price to maximize early profit). This is one of the most frequently tested pairs in marketing.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Pricing strategies include penetration (low price for market entry), skimming (high price for early profit), cost-plus (cost + markup), and competitive pricing (matching rivals). Pricing decisions are shaped by costs, competition, customer ability to pay, regulation, and product life cycle stage.\n</div>\n  ',
