    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Sales promotion</span> covers short-term incentives designed to encourage the quick purchase of a product or service, complementing longer-term efforts like advertising and branding.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Sales promotion involves activities, other than personal selling, advertising, and public relations, that stimulate consumer purchasing and dealer effectiveness through short-term incentives designed to encourage immediate sales.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Methods of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Discounts</td><td>Temporary price reductions to encourage purchase</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coupons</td><td>Certificates giving buyers a price reduction on a specific product</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Free samples</td><td>Giving a small quantity of a product free to encourage trial</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Exhibitions/trade fairs</td><td>Events where businesses display and demonstrate products to potential buyers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contests/sweepstakes</td><td>Prize-based promotions to boost engagement and purchase</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Importance of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Sales promotion boosts short-term sales, encourages trial of new products, helps clear excess inventory, attracts customers away from competitors, and builds excitement/urgency around a purchase.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Limitations of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Overuse can devalue a brand (making customers only buy when discounted), may only produce temporary sales spikes rather than long-term loyalty, can be costly, and may attract price-sensitive "deal hunters" who are not loyal long-term customers.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember sales promotion is meant to be SHORT-TERM, unlike advertising and branding which build long-term image. Confusing the two is a common exam error.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Sales promotion uses short-term incentives — discounts, coupons, free samples, exhibitions — to stimulate immediate purchases and clear inventory, but overuse can devalue a brand and fails to build the long-term loyalty that advertising and branding achieve.\n</div>\n  ',
