    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Advertising</span> is a paid, non-personal form of communication used to inform, persuade, and remind consumers about a product, service, or idea through various media channels.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Advertising</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Advertising is any paid form of non-personal presentation and promotion of ideas, goods, or services by an identified sponsor, delivered through media such as television, radio, newspapers, billboards, and the internet.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Types of Advertising Media</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Print</td><td>Newspapers, magazines, flyers, posters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Broadcast</td><td>Television and radio commercials</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Outdoor</td><td>Billboards, banners, transit (bus/vehicle) ads</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Online</td><td>Social media ads, search engine ads, website banners, influencer marketing</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Importance of Advertising</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Advertising builds product awareness and brand recognition, informs consumers about product features and benefits, persuades customers to choose one brand over competitors, reminds existing customers to keep buying, and supports overall business growth and revenue.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Limitations of Advertising</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Advertising can be expensive (especially TV/broadcast), may not guarantee sales despite the cost, can be ignored or skipped by audiences (ad fatigue), may be misleading if not regulated properly, and its effectiveness can be hard to measure precisely.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Note the key phrase in the definition: advertising is "paid" and "non-personal" — this distinguishes it from personal selling (which is direct/personal) and public relations (which is often unpaid/earned media).\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Advertising is paid, non-personal promotion through media like print, broadcast, outdoor, and online channels. It builds awareness, informs, and persuades customers, though it can be costly and its impact on actual sales can be difficult to measure precisely.\n</div>\n  ',
