    term: 'Third Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Personal selling</span> is the face-to-face (or direct one-on-one) presentation of a product by a salesperson to a prospective buyer, with the goal of making a sale.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Personal Selling</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Personal selling involves direct, personal communication between a salesperson and a potential customer, allowing for immediate feedback, tailored persuasion, and relationship-building that mass advertising cannot achieve.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Qualities of a Good Salesperson</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Quality</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Product knowledge</td><td>Answers customer questions confidently and accurately</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Good communication skills</td><td>Clearly explains benefits and listens to customer needs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Patience and persistence</td><td>Follows up with customers without being pushy</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Honesty/integrity</td><td>Builds long-term trust rather than one-time sales</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Good appearance and manners</td><td>Creates a positive first impression</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Importance of Personal Selling</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Personal selling allows for two-way communication (answering questions immediately), builds strong personal relationships and trust, allows the sales pitch to be customized to each customer\'s specific needs, and can close complex or high-value sales that advertising alone cannot achieve.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Challenges of Personal Selling</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Personal selling can be costly (salaries, commissions, training), time-consuming since it reaches one customer at a time, dependent on the skill of individual salespeople (inconsistent quality), and salespeople may face rejection frequently, which can be demoralizing.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember: personal selling is the ONLY promotional tool involving direct, two-way, personal interaction — this is what distinguishes it from advertising and sales promotion.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Personal selling is direct, one-on-one communication between a salesperson and a customer, requiring qualities like product knowledge, communication skill, and honesty. It builds trust and closes complex sales but is costly and time-consuming compared to mass promotional methods.\n</div>\n  ',
