    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Consumer protection</span> refers to laws, regulations, and organizations designed to safeguard the rights and interests of consumers against unfair, deceptive, or fraudulent business practices.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Consumer Protection</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Consumer protection encompasses the measures put in place by government, agencies, and organizations to ensure consumers are treated fairly, receive accurate information, and are protected from exploitation, unsafe products, and fraud in the marketplace.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Basic Rights of Consumers</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Right</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Right to safety</td><td>Protection against products/services hazardous to health or life</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Right to information</td><td>Access to accurate information needed to make informed choices</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Right to choose</td><td>Access to a variety of products/services at competitive prices</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Right to be heard</td><td>Consumer interests receive fair consideration in policy-making and complaint handling</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Right to redress</td><td>Fair settlement of legitimate complaints, including compensation for harm</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Bodies/Agencies Responsible for Consumer Protection in Nigeria</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Key agencies include the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Commission (FCCPC), the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC) for food/drug safety, the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) for product quality standards, and consumer advocacy/civil society groups.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Common Unfair Trade Practices</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">These include false or misleading advertising, selling substandard/expired goods, short-changing customers, hoarding to create artificial scarcity, price gouging, and selling counterfeit products.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Memorize the five basic consumer rights and be ready to match each right to a real-life scenario — this is a frequently tested format.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Consumer protection safeguards consumers\' rights to safety, information, choice, being heard, and redress. Agencies like FCCPC, NAFDAC, and SON enforce these protections against unfair trade practices such as false advertising and sale of substandard goods.\n</div>\n  ',
