      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Marketing is a dynamic field that keeps evolving. <span class="learn-keyword">Contemporary issues</span> refer to current trends, challenges, and developments reshaping how goods and services are marketed today.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Digital Transformation and E-commerce</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The rise of online shopping, mobile commerce, and digital payment platforms has transformed how consumers discover, evaluate, and purchase products, forcing traditional businesses to adapt or risk losing market share.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Key Contemporary Issues</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Social media marketing</td><td>Businesses now market directly to consumers through platforms like Instagram, TikTok, and Facebook</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Influencer marketing</td><td>Using popular online personalities to promote products to their followers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Green/sustainable marketing</td><td>Growing consumer demand for environmentally friendly products and practices</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data privacy concerns</td><td>Increasing consumer worry about how companies collect and use their personal data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Globalization</td><td>Increased competition from international brands entering local markets</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Impact of Globalization on Local Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Globalization has increased competition as foreign brands enter local markets, but it has also opened new export opportunities for local businesses, exposed consumers to a wider variety of products, and pushed local companies to improve quality and innovation to remain competitive.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Ethical Issues in Modern Marketing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Modern marketers face growing scrutiny over issues such as truthful advertising, responsible use of consumer data, avoiding manipulative marketing to vulnerable groups (e.g., children), and demonstrating genuine environmental/social responsibility rather than superficial "greenwashing."</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners often ask you to relate contemporary issues to real Nigerian examples — e.g., the growth of online shopping platforms and social media-based businesses.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Contemporary marketing issues include digital transformation and e-commerce, social media and influencer marketing, growing demand for sustainable products, data privacy concerns, and the effects of globalization on local businesses and competition.\n</div>\n  ',
