    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Marketing offers a wide range of <span class="learn-keyword">career opportunities</span> for students, from creative roles in advertising to analytical roles in market research and everything in between.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of a Marketing Career</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A marketing career involves working in roles focused on understanding customer needs, promoting products/services, managing sales, and building brand relationships within a business or organization.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Examples of Marketing Careers</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Career</th><th>Typical Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Sales Representative</td><td>Directly sells products/services to customers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Brand Manager</td><td>Oversees the image, positioning, and performance of a specific brand</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Market Researcher</td><td>Studies consumer behavior and market trends to guide business decisions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Advertising Executive</td><td>Plans and creates advertising campaigns for clients</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Public Relations Officer</td><td>Manages an organization\'s image and media relationships</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Digital Marketing Specialist</td><td>Manages online marketing, social media, and e-commerce campaigns</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Skills and Qualifications Needed</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Successful marketing careers typically require strong communication skills, creativity, analytical/research ability, understanding of consumer behavior, digital literacy (for modern roles), and often a relevant degree or professional certification in marketing, business administration, or a related field.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Prospects and Importance of Marketing Careers</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Marketing careers offer strong growth prospects as businesses of all sizes need marketing expertise, opportunities for entrepreneurship (starting one\'s own marketing agency), diverse specializations to match different interests and skills, and increasing demand for digital marketing skills in today\'s economy.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners may ask you to match a career title to its main responsibility (e.g., Brand Manager → brand image/positioning). Study the table above carefully.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Marketing offers diverse career paths — sales, brand management, market research, advertising, PR, and digital marketing — each requiring specific skills like communication, creativity, and analytical ability. Growing demand, especially for digital skills, makes marketing a promising career field.\n</div>\n  ',
